<title>MEXICO: Mexico's Pemex details 1996 hydrocarbon trade.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Pemex details 1996 hydrocarbon trade.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's oil and gas monopoly Petroleos Mexicanos (Pemex) reported its exports and imports of crude oil, petroleum products, natural gas and chemicals for 1996. Figures in millions of dollars.</p>
<p>    Item		     1995		  1996</p>
<p>    Balance		 7,195		 9,962</p>
<p>	Exports	     8,401		11,609</p>
<p>	Imports	     1,206		 1,647</p>
<p>    Crude Exports	 7,480		10,705</p>
<p>    Petroleum Products   -586		-1,140</p>
<p>	Exports		 489		   416</p>
<p>	Imports	     1,075		 1,555</p>
<p>    Natural Gas	     -87		   -35</p>
<p>	Exports		  12		    32</p>
<p>	Imports		  99		    67</p>
<p>    Petrochemicals	  388		   432</p>
<p>	Exports		 420		   457</p>
<p>	Imports		  32		    25</p>
<p>((--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903))</p>
